      "Language": "swe",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The positive effects of cholesterol-lowering therapy in coronary artery disease are well recognised. This study, on 99 consecutive coronary artery bypass grafted patients, shows that an intensive one-year follow-up at a secondary prevention specialist clinic significantly improves cholesterol levels compared to conventional follow-up in the primary health care system. However, these positive results are not consistent after a 2.6 year return to the primary health care. Consequently, improved collaboration between hospital and primary health care physicians in the development of structured secondary prevention programmes is essential."},
